  "hypothesis": "measured (M4, same process, identical results, 2026-11-05): ranking from the mapped checkpoint is 1.5x to 1.9x slower than from the live store on all four corpora. On FiQA the flat varint postings cost most of it: 56% of postings carry a frequency above 1 and missed the one-byte fast path; the two-byte window decoder recovers 1.09x, and the rest needs a block-packed checkpoint posting encoding (a checkpoint format change). On the small corpora, rebuilding a StoredDocument per hit (record decode, JSON metadata, clone, drop) is about 45% of a query. Block-max MaxScore was slower than the exhaustive pass at k=100, and a larger hot-list budget doubles serving RSS",
  "code_path": "src/core/documents.rs (prepare, search), src/core/documents/search.rs, src/core/engine/document_api.rs"
 },
